{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "tours/04-invoke-grpc",
  "nextTour": "tours/05-observer-grpc",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "orders/orders-domain/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/orders/domain/OrderService.java",
      "description": "This tour follows the same call when the `grpc` Spring profile is active.\n`OrderService` is unchanged: it invokes `CustomerCreditService`.",
      "line": 28
    },
    {
      "file": "orders/orders-credit-management-grpc-proxy/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/orders/creditmanagement/grpcproxy/CreditManagementGrpcProxyConfiguration.java",
      "description": "With the `grpc` profile active, `CustomerCreditService` is implemented by `CreditManagementGrpcProxy`, which is in the `orders-credit-management-grpc-proxy` Gradle subproject.\nIt calls the `customers` domain's in-process gRPC server through a channel that uses `directExecutor()`.",
      "line": 18
    },
    {
      "file": "orders/orders-credit-management-grpc-proxy/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/orders/creditmanagement/grpcproxy/CreditManagementGrpcProxy.java",
      "description": "`CreditManagementGrpcProxy` converts the arguments to a `ReserveCreditRequest` and calls a blocking stub.\nA blocking stub returns only after the server has finished, so the call stays inside the caller's transaction.",
      "line": 25
    },
    {
      "file": "customers/customers-api-credit-management-grpc/src/main/proto/credit_management.proto",
      "description": "`ReserveCredit` is defined in `credit_management.proto`, in the `customers-api-credit-management-grpc` Gradle subproject.\nIt's the gRPC version of the `customers` domain's credit management API.\n\nThe protobuf Gradle plugin generates the message classes and `CreditManagementServiceGrpc` from this file.",
      "line": 12
    },
    {
      "file": "customers/customers-credit-management-grpc-server/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/customers/creditmanagement/grpcserver/CreditManagementGrpcServerConfiguration.java",
      "description": "The `customers-credit-management-grpc-server` Gradle subproject starts an in-process gRPC server.\n`directExecutor()` runs each call on the caller's thread, so it joins the caller's transaction.",
      "line": 26
    },
    {
      "file": "customers/customers-credit-management-grpc-server/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/customers/creditmanagement/grpcserver/CreditManagementGrpcService.java",
      "description": "`CreditManagementGrpcService` extends the generated `CreditManagementServiceImplBase`.\nIts `reserveCredit()` method invokes the `CreditManagement` interface.",
      "line": 29
    },
    {
      "file": "customers/customers-credit-management-grpc-server/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/customers/creditmanagement/grpcserver/CreditManagementGrpcService.java",
      "description": "Exceptions are mapped to gRPC status codes: `NOT_FOUND` for an unknown customer, `FAILED_PRECONDITION` when the credit limit is exceeded.\nThe proxy throws `StatusRuntimeException` for an error status, which rolls back the caller's transaction.",
      "line": 71
    },
    {
      "file": "customers/customers-domain/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/customers/domain/CustomerServiceImpl.java",
      "description": "`CreditManagement` is implemented by `CustomerServiceImpl`, just as in the POJO version.",
      "line": 55
    },
    {
      "file": "orders/orders-domain/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/orders/domain/OrderService.java",
      "description": "After reserving credit, `OrderService` calls `NotificationSender` to send an order confirmation email.",
      "line": 31
    },
    {
      "file": "orders/orders-notifications-grpc-proxy/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/orders/notifications/grpcproxy/NotificationGrpcProxy.java",
      "description": "With the `grpc` profile active, `NotificationSender` is implemented by `NotificationGrpcProxy`, in the `orders-notifications-grpc-proxy` Gradle subproject.\nProtobuf has no type for an arbitrary Java object, so it converts each template parameter with `String.valueOf()`.",
      "line": 27
    },
    {
      "file": "notifications/notifications-api-grpc/src/main/proto/notifications.proto",
      "description": "`notifications.proto`, in the `notifications-api-grpc` Gradle subproject, defines the template parameters as a `map<string, string>`.",
      "line": 18
    },
    {
      "file": "notifications/notifications-grpc-server/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/notifications/grpcserver/NotificationGrpcService.java",
      "description": "`NotificationGrpcService`, in the `notifications-grpc-server` Gradle subproject, invokes the POJO `NotificationService`.\nLike the credit management server, it runs on the caller's thread, inside the caller's transaction.",
      "line": 25
    },
    {
      "file": "notifications/notifications-domain/src/main/java/net/chrisrichardson/examples/monolithiccustomersandorders/notifications/domain/NotificationServiceImpl.java",
      "description": "`NotificationService` is implemented by `NotificationServiceImpl`, just as in the POJO version.",
      "line": 11
    }
  ],
  "ref": "main"
}
